{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae","id":910526,"title":"What First Comes To Your Mind When You Think Of The True Fae?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-08T20:51:01-07:00","id":910526,"title":"What First Comes To Your Mind When You Think Of The True Fae?","content":"For me, the first mental image is usually a tall and elvish jester of sorts, with a Mien like <a href=\"http://www.mariowiki.com/images/thumb/a/a0/DimentioSuperPaperMario.png/200px-DimentioSuperPaperMario.png\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Dimentio</b></a> and a laughter like that of the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q1lM_kyNjRU\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Skull Kid.</b></a><br /> <br /> After that, I think of figures like the Slender Man (especially as portrayed <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q2duevcUMGw\" target=\"_blank\"><b>here</b></a>), GLaDOS and the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=USZGm9GR7ak\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Mysterious Stranger</b></a>.<br /> <br /> When it comes to their bargains, I often think of Dr. Facilier and Ursula. More specifically, I imagine them singing &quot;Friends On The Other Side&quot; and &quot;Poor And Unfortunate Souls&quot;, respectively.<br /> <br /> So, I guess my favorite True Fae tend to be like Disney villains to some degree, but with a strong eldritch dose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T21:24:02-07:00","id":910547,"title":"","content":"Depends on where they are, broadly speaking. Outside of Faerie the adjective I'd use to describe the commonality of their builds is &quot;insubstantial.&quot;<br /> <br /> As an aside, the title of this thread is coincidentally relevant to the Underwood freehold of Chicago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T21:30:13-07:00","id":910551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=910547#post910547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on where they are, broadly speaking. Outside of Faerie the adjective I'd use to describe the commonality of their builds is &amp;quot;insubstantial.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> As an aside, the title of this thread is coincidentally relevant to the Underwood freehold of Chicago.</div> </div> </div> </div> Insubstantial how? Are they a little transparent and protean?<br /> <br /> I don't remember where this Freehold is written. Can you please tell me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T21:50:40-07:00","id":910562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=910551#post910551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Insubstantial how? Are they a little transparent and protean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Small or thin or not all there, though the needs of subtlety tend to confine the third to personal encounters and sneakery.<br /> <br /> Spiderleg hands and feet of fog and all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't remember where this Freehold is written. Can you please tell me? </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=847386#post847386\">The freehold didn't have a proper name when it was last discussed in public</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T06:42:37-07:00","id":910734,"title":"","content":"I think of what would happen if cthulhu hollowed out Tinkerbell, The Wizard of Oz, the big bad wolf, Snow White, Little Red Riding Hood, the Enchanted Forest, and Zues, and then wore them all like a suit of clothing, and tried to play their roles, and was bound up by the wyrd in the process.<br /> <br /> Think under all the Fairy Tale indentities is something alien and terrifying, something none fae, that uses fairy tales or stories as a way of interacting with a level of reality it doesn't really understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:02:35-07:00","id":910747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=910734#post910734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think of what would happen if cthulhu hollowed out Tinkerbell, The Wizard of Oz, the big bad wolf, Snow White, Little Red Riding Hood, the Enchanted Forest, and Zues, and then wore them all like a suit of clothing, and tried to play their roles, and was bound up by the wyrd in the process.<br /> <br /> Think under all the Fairy Tale indentities is something alien and terrifying, something none fae, that uses fairy tales or stories as a way of interacting with a level of reality it doesn't really understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm just imagining a cosmic horror from beyond using the above characters as sock puppets on the end of its tentacles or whatever. So... mission accomplished?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:37:51-07:00","id":910772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=910747#post910747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now I'm just imagining a cosmic horror from beyond using the above characters as sock puppets on the end of its tentacles or whatever. So... mission accomplished?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not exactly, these cosmic horrors don't have forms, naked humans can percieve them or conceptualize them, making them more alien the most Lovecraftian Gods, so they make deals with the Wyrd in Arcadia, to gain titles and once they have titles, to interact with stuff, and only then do they have forms as humans know it, but those fairy tail forms are just a custome the alien being puts on.<br /> <br /> So maybe you think your dealing with Tinkerbell the True Fae and she acts like on would expect Tinkerbell to act, mostly if on the extreme side, but there awrongness born of have no real understanding, because Tinkerbell has the soul of an alien cosmic horror that still stuggles to understand the world beyond its roles.<br /> <br /> So it does weird hurtful things not really grasping the meaning of what it does.<br /> <br /> It why it can be Tinkbell, Neverland, and Peter Pan's Sword all at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:14:59-07:00","id":910915,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://fhif.wikia.com/wiki/World\" target=\"_blank\">World</a>, from<i> &quot;Foster's Home for Imaginary Friends&quot;</i> last episode, could be a good example of a Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 06-09-2016, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:29:43-07:00","id":910932,"title":"","content":"I typically like to keep my Gentry vague when describing them in games I am running, but if you are asking what comes to mind..<br /> <br /> I would say something like Satan from the film Adventures of Mark Twain (1985). A strangely dressed body with no head, holding a mask that emotes and moves when the being speaks. It has the power to alter its own little corner of reality, and seems to have thoughts and opinions that clash against the status quo. Unknowable, alien, horrific or beautiful, perhaps both. Always an air of magic about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11942-the13thghost","name":"The13thGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:36:02-07:00","id":910988,"title":"","content":"Madoka Witches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:37:57-07:00","id":911044,"title":"","content":"Mary Sues.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the story is all about them, everything else in the story exists to give them an opportunity to prove how great they are. And when I say &quot;story&quot; I mean story as in &quot;<u>Story</u>teller system&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you are enslaved by or even get too close to a True Fae then you become a secondary charachter in their story. You are no longer Alice, with her own Aspirations and story. You're just the arm candy that proves what a manly man the True Fae is. Or you're the witch the True Fae kills to prove how heroic he is.<br /> <br /> But there is room to manoeuvrer within the confines of the role. The arm candy cannot leave or do anything that might emasculate the True Fae, but she could take a younger and prettier ward and escape through being discarded*. The witch cannot hide from the True Fae's persuit, nor can she defeat him in their climactic confrontation. But she could brew five cunning curses in her cauldron and carve a champion for each, and a final climatic champion to stand over the likeness of her dead body then escape while the True Fae is busy with his heroic quest to break the curses**.<br /> <br /> * Darkling Seeming.<br /> ** Wizened Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:53:22-07:00","id":911260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=911044#post911044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mary Sues.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the story is all about them, everything else in the story exists to give them an opportunity to prove how great they are. And when I say &amp;quot;story&amp;quot; I mean story as in &amp;quot;<u>Story</u>teller system&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> If you are enslaved by or even get too close to a True Fae then you become a secondary charachter in their story. You are no longer Alice, with her own Aspirations and story. You're just the arm candy that proves what a manly man the True Fae is. Or you're the witch the True Fae kills to prove how heroic he is.<br /> <br /> But there is room to manoeuvrer within the confines of the role. The arm candy cannot leave or do anything that might emasculate the True Fae, but she could take a younger and prettier ward and escape through being discarded*. The witch cannot hide from the True Fae's persuit, nor can she defeat him in their climactic confrontation. But she could brew five cunning curses in her cauldron and carve a champion for each, and a final climatic champion to stand over the likeness of her dead body then escape while the True Fae is busy with his heroic quest to break the curses**.<br /> <br /> * Darkling Seeming.<br /> ** Wizened Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div> I really like this. Mary Sues, inciteful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:41:08-07:00","id":911385,"title":"","content":"Deranged ,Aloof, Charlatans / and Royalty. To Monstrous beast from old folklore. Alien beings that merge with the dreams and nightmares of humanity. Can they be reasoned with? No, only bartered or negotiated with at best. And it better be something to their liking. Gotta play on their wants and curiosities, if you can. But Ultimately you can never trust them.<br /> <br /> Certain characters come to mind like. Hades, &quot;The Beast&quot; from Into the Unknown, Master Mirror O'Dimm from Witcher 3, Mr. Mxyzptlk from DC Comics .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:25:40-07:00","id":911462,"title":"","content":"A being bound by their own tale who can only act as their role allows and as such they are confined and can not grow beyond their role. That is why they prize changelings because they themselves can not do the wonders a human can, the true fae lack the freedom to chose their path. What there were will always be what they are, any apparent change is not true change but the flow of the story. The true fae only exist within the confines of their story and can never live as they wish to if this wish falls outside of their story.<br /> <br /> however I may be wrong, I haven't read all too much about the true fey and more just skimmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T05:56:00-07:00","id":911594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=911044#post911044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mary Sues.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the story is all about them, everything else in the story exists to give them an opportunity to prove how great they are. And when I say &quot;story&quot; I mean story as in &quot;<u>Story</u>teller system&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you are enslaved by or even get too close to a True Fae then you become a secondary charachter in their story. You are no longer Alice, with her own Aspirations and story. You're just the arm candy that proves what a manly man the True Fae is. Or you're the witch the True Fae kills to prove how heroic he is.<br /> <br /> But there is room to manoeuvrer within the confines of the role. The arm candy cannot leave or do anything that might emasculate the True Fae, but she could take a younger and prettier ward and escape through being discarded*. The witch cannot hide from the True Fae's persuit, nor can she defeat him in their climactic confrontation. But she could brew five cunning curses in her cauldron and carve a champion for each, and a final climatic champion to stand over the likeness of her dead body then escape while the True Fae is busy with his heroic quest to break the curses**.<br /> <br /> * Darkling Seeming.<br /> ** Wizened Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely an aspect I'm working with in regards to Ziggy and his former Keeper, Helvetica. Helvetica's taken up the narrative that she's the noble warrior fighting the villainous sorcerer who hides behind minions (the freehold/Autumn court). It's become a part of Ziggy's Personal Approach: A huntsman gains Yearning if they force him to act directly or expose himself to protect his 'game pieces.' As long as he can keep throwing spells, curses, and &quot;minions&quot; at Helvetica and her huntsman, she can't attack him directly. As a consequence, Ziggy is very careful to warn subordinates about the dangers of working for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T11:58:15-07:00","id":914251,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://images-cdn.moviepilot.com/images/c_fill,h_588,w_1140/t_mp_quality/ojbphppiqp7ubgbhcy5r/bill-cipher-s-secrets-revealed-what-you-need-to-know-before-gravity-falls-s02e18-gravit-676137.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Let's Make a Deal!</b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T15:21:03-07:00","id":914419,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> Agreed wholeheartedly.<br /> <br /> I forgot to mention that, in terms of Titles in Wisp form, I usually think of the Gentlemen from the Buffy episode &quot;Hush&quot;...and the Robot Masters from Megaman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T17:44:52-07:00","id":914489,"title":"","content":"In terms of what we envision as the &quot;archetypal&quot; True Fae, whenever I think of the gentry my initial mental image is a sort of horned god-type figure- a towering man with massive antlers clad in bark and leaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T04:24:07-07:00","id":914742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=914489#post914489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of what we envision as the &quot;archetypal&quot; True Fae, whenever I think of the gentry my initial mental image is a sort of horned god-type figure- a towering man with massive antlers clad in bark and leaves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You mean like this guy?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/age-of-wonders-3/images/7/77/Art_Horned_God.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20141022135957\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:53:26-07:00","id":914955,"title":"","content":"I am reminded of this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iR5pZfP.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T15:16:25-07:00","id":915123,"title":"","content":"A possible realm in Arcadia:<br /> <br /> &quot;We had a saying, 'when everything changes, nothing changes.' But all this, this isn't what we had in mind. This town. It changes shape all the time, right? Bridges, parks, highways rising, falling. Rising and falling. At the peoples' whim. With the changing of the seasons. Even the seasons, they're just... whim.&quot;<br /> <br /> -<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0DviyuGNeWc\" target=\"_blank\">Royce Bracket, Transistor</a>. (For those who haven't played, the rest is spoilery.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T17:57:01-07:00","id":915221,"title":"","content":"I've seen multiple awesome writeups of Peter as a True Fae, and I recommend the original book to literally anyone who's interested in Changeling, so I'm seconding that very hard. <br /> <br /> The reason the &quot;horned god&quot; image sticks out to me is probably because the illustration of a True Fae in the 1e core has antlers (though it's way weirder) and my association of the &quot;big guy with antlers&quot; image and the idea of an archetypal pagan nature-god, like the kind of True Fae who's had cave paintings made of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:18:26-07:00","id":915619,"title":"","content":"Ever since I read Jonathan Strange &amp; Mr. Norrell, nothing has struck me as more archetypal of a classic British True Fae than The Gentleman With The Thistledown Hair. I'm pretty sure that he's even listed as an inspiration in the corebook. His powers are literally described as deriving from ancient contracts with the elements of nature and reality itself. Not to mention his alien morality, penchant for stealing people and twisted, murderous fairy godmother act.<br /> <br /> In more general terms, I think of them as fanfic writers. They can only love people in the way that a fan loves their favorite character. They are fascinated by them and want to put through interesting (read: traumatic) stories for their entertainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:40:53-07:00","id":915817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=915619#post915619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In more general terms, I think of them as fanfic writers. They can only love people in the way that a fan loves their favorite character. They are fascinated by them and want to put through interesting (read: traumatic) stories for their entertainment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, fanfic writers do love to add excessive levels of drama to their stories and force characters to act out of the ordinary for their own satisfaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T16:42:20-07:00","id":916486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=915817#post915817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, fanfic writers do love to add excessive levels of drama to their stories and force characters to act out of the ordinary for their own satisfaction.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's part of the fun of fan fiction, getting to play &quot;god&quot; with your favourite characters and having things go the way you fantasize (even if its something you'd never support in real life).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T17:08:03-07:00","id":916497,"title":"","content":"Elves. Or the sidhe or eladrin or whatever the fantasy setting wants to call the immortal beautiful people.<br /> <br /> I get they can be anything and none of my games played up elven looks, those seeming more like a robot boss, the Triple Goddess, a titan, a lich, and Popeye. But the term alone makes me think in that direction the way people think of red-skinned bat-winged evils when they hear Demon, and a lot of the imagery in the books shows sort of elvish features, tall or slender beings with pointed ears..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-17-2016, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T20:39:04-07:00","id":916604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=916486#post916486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's part of the fun of fan fiction, getting to play &quot;god&quot; with your favourite characters and having things go the way you fantasize (even if its something you'd never support in real life).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Except once you read enough, you realize every fanfic is virtually identical in terms of plot, character concepts, and behavior. They start to follow a recognized pattern.<br /> <br /> Fanfic writers have no originality, just like the True Fae!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T21:07:22-07:00","id":916622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=916604#post916604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except once you read enough, you realize every fanfic is virtually identical in terms of plot, character concepts, and behavior. They start to follow a recognized pattern.<br /> <br /> Fanfic writers have no originality, just like the True Fae!</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who spent most of their first decade on the internet lurking on fanfiction boards, this is colossally disingenuous.<br /> <br /> A lot of them are children, which <i>is</i> a point of commonality with the Others, but when you're a living self-narrating story without a soul it's kind of hard to avoid getting tropey, especially when it's part of your nature to make things adhere to narrative rules regardless of how long you've been in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T21:44:46-07:00","id":916640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=916622#post916622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as someone who spent most of their first decade on the internet lurking on fanfiction boards, this is colossally disingenuous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stop me if you've heard this plot summary before...<br /> <br /> 1. Mary Sue, self insertion<br /> <br /> 2. Canon characters falling in love with Mary Sue self insertion.<br /> <br /> 3. Canon characters falling in love with each other, even though they have no prior chemistry to suggest doing so.<br /> <br /> 4. An absurdly powerful, stupidly evil villain who may or may not be an allegory for Satan, himself.<br /> <br /> 5. Swearing, lots and lots of fucking swearing. Because we're grown ups, god damn it!<br /> <br /> 6. Dragon Ball style power up for the main protagonist, because the author made the villain too powerful to defeat in a convincing way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>And by the way, that's all in the same story... and about 20 other fanfics I read early in my internet days.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Like I said, no originality. They're just retelling what they've already seen before, but trying to put their own spin on it, so we can clap for them and tell them how talented they are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-18-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T21:52:54-07:00","id":916646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=916640#post916640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stop me if you've heard this plot summary before...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nyr?<br /> <br /> Neither remotely the point nor even broadly likely to win you points.<br /> <br /> Children. You're mocking a story structure used by literal children.<br /> <br /> And comparing them to monsters that have no small number of abuser-metaphors among them.<br /> <br /> You're breaking no new ground and doing nobody any favors, least of all yourself.<br /> <br /> Drop it. It's not witty or funny or even a little bit clever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T22:17:04-07:00","id":916660,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Yeah, let's do drop this line of discussion. Fan fiction writers are a group, attacking them is against the rules.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T22:29:17-07:00","id":916663,"title":"","content":"When the True Fey are mentioned without a specific identity I tend to visualize a shadowy silhouette holding many masks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T22:34:37-07:00","id":916664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=916646#post916646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nyr?<br /> <br /> Neither remotely the point nor even broadly likely to win you points.<br /> <br /> Children. You're mocking a story structure used by literal children.<br /> <br /> And comparing them to monsters that have no small number of abuser-metaphors among them.<br /> <br /> You're breaking no new ground and doing nobody any favors, least of all yourself.<br /> <br /> Drop it. It's not witty or funny or even a little bit clever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wasn't aware I was trying to win anything. I was just following up a comparison somebody else made before me. And as for the abuser-metaphors, I think it's been a while since you read your last fanfic. Because I can guarantee you that the children writing the stories seem to enjoy making the characters go through hell because they think it will make the story better reading material.There's a reason I said the villain is stupidly evil and may be an allegory for Satan. They aren't just take-over-the-world type of evil, they're rape-and-pillage style of evil who exhibit demonic powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was merely agreeing with the comparison between fanfictions themselves and the way in which the True Fae operate. The True Fae is the author, and everyone else are the characters playing the script written out for them.<br /> <br /> Wasn't trying to pick on the kids or any particular group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T22:39:33-07:00","id":916666,"title":"","content":"Aaaand, seems Charlaquin's post was written while I was submitting my last response. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T00:15:33-07:00","id":916695,"title":"","content":"Honestly it just sounds like you've had a particularly unfortunate run of bad fanfics or possibly need to find a better venue than wherever your currently reading them. Like everything on the internet, some fanfics are terrible and some of them are great. Some of them are by the numbers cliches, and some of them are quite unique. <br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> The True Fae are like watching a movie in a language you do not understand without any translation. You can glean some information by context and observation, but there are whole portions of the whole picture that are simply impossible to understand. That's how the Fae should be (to my mind). Their actions are their own, and while some portions of their goals should be made manifest (the lady with the violent eyes seeks the moon rose that blooms once every hundred years on the site of a bloody battlefield) part of their existence should never be revealed or be entirely alien (e.g.- what does she even need with the rose? Why does she seem satisfied when the characters thwart her attempts to retrieve it?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T00:20:32-07:00","id":916697,"title":"","content":"True Fae can't really be bundled under a single group, really. They're all different, even if they have similar/overarching methods and ideas. Keepers can be pleasant beings, but only so long as you agree with their pleasantness; being trapped in a gingerbread house that always feeds you can be hell to those who hate sugar, or want to go outside, for example, but heaven for those who love sweets and just want to keep eating it. The Keeper could be genuinely ignorant about your own wants/dislikes (after all, who wants to not have some of their plum pudding all the time) or cruel about it (you'd eat and eat and eat until you exploded because they want that), but the point is that they perceive what you want as being what they want, and in their eyes what goes against that is wrong or inconceivable enough to warrant them &quot;fixing&quot; you.<br /> <br /> ...of course, there are those who subvert that too. Saying all True Fae act in the same way, outside of being alien, is underestimating them. Otherwise Changelings would have an easier time dealing with True Fae.<br /> <br /> (my original post had me comparing them to people with dementia; this was in poor taste, and it was partially fueled by an ugly confrontation with my grandma who has the condition and became confused when she was here during a visit to see her family, hence the rework)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 06-18-2016, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T12:19:04-07:00","id":916940,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://img06.deviantart.net/8270/i/2013/174/3/d/skull_kid_and_the_moon_by_nekokyandichan-d6acty4.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">when you're the bad guy, you just run</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T13:05:09-07:00","id":916954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=916940#post916940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"http://img06.deviantart.net/8270/i/2013/174/3/d/skull_kid_and_the_moon_by_nekokyandichan-d6acty4.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">when you're the bad guy, you just run</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That coincides quite nicely with a Gentry idea I had already, where the moon of the realm was both the gentry's eye and her home; all within her domain were pretty much to do as much magic and mayhem within it, using each other for test subjects so she may incorporate their tricks into her own repetoir. She was known as The Our of Witching. I should look into finding more images like that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T16:17:47-07:00","id":917025,"title":"","content":"The beauty of the True Fae is that they aren't just solipsistic god-children from another world. They ARE stories made real, beautiful lies made real and sustained through Glamour. Their titles define their purpose and give them form, and the Wyrd is the cosmic Storyteller that binds them all to their endless games against one another. <br /> <br /> But that wasn't the question posted, I just couldn't help myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To me the first image that pops into my head when someone mentions the True Fae is the Other Mother from Lyka's Coraline. Next come Peter Pan from Once Upon A Time, and finally the House, mechanisms, and staff from Cabin in the Woods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 06-19-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T16:32:14-07:00","id":917031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=916640#post916640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Stop me if you've heard this plot summary before...<br /> <br /> 1. Mary Sue, self insertion<br /> <br /> 2. Canon characters falling in love with Mary Sue self insertion.<br /> <br /> 3. Canon characters falling in love with each other, even though they have no prior chemistry to suggest doing so.<br /> <br /> 4. An absurdly powerful, stupidly evil villain who may or may not be an allegory for Satan, himself.<br /> <br /> 5. Swearing, lots and lots of fucking swearing. Because we're grown ups, god damn it!<br /> <br /> 6. Dragon Ball style power up for the main protagonist, because the author made the villain too powerful to defeat in a convincing way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>And by the way, that's all in the same story... and about 20 other fanfics I read early in my internet days.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Like I said, no originality. They're just retelling what they've already seen before, but trying to put their own spin on it, so we can clap for them and tell them how talented they are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Yes I've read those, but I've read some really good stuff too, gripping stuff, like star trek fan fiction, Broken Boudice (no link, because its X-Rated).<br /> <br /> I have done fan insert story, but no one fell in love with my character, I was the insane evil villian who did really weird, delusional, super villiany stuff.<br /> <br /> But its was a comic book fic, but am I did introduce an awesome character of my own, a fictional daughter who had three brains/minds/personalities, two of which were contained in her breasts.<br /> <br /> They each had a different telekinetic power, Telekenisis, Pyrokenisis, and Cyrokenisis, but they argued with each other all the time, except when they combined briefly to one mind, which had the power of telepathic mental projection, but what was an insane, unpredictable and dangerous personality.<br /> <br /> Sorry about the thread drift, I just had to respond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 06-18-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T18:28:00-07:00","id":917078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=917031#post917031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I've read those, but I've read some really good stuff too, gripping stuff, like star trek fan fiction, Broken Boudice (no link, because its X-Rated).<br /> <br /> I have done fan insert story, but no one fell in love with my character, I was the insane evil villian who did really weird, delusional, super villiany stuff.<br /> <br /> But its was a comic book fic, but am I did introduce an awesome character of my own, a fictional daughter who had three brains/minds/personalities, two of which were contained in her breasts.<br /> <br /> They each had a different telekinetic power, Telekenisis, Pyrokenisis, and Cyrokenisis, but they argued with each other all the time, except when they combined briefly to one mind, which had the power of telepathic mental projection, but what was an insane, unpredictable and dangerous personality.<br /> <br /> Sorry about the thread drift, I just had to respond.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well that sounds friggin awesome, but this argument has been taken to the PM's to avoid causing any further drama.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, here's Bill Cipher doing some Fae related shenanigans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_9CY_B5hLo\" data-code=\"r_9CY_B5hLo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/r_9CY_B5hLo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T20:22:01-07:00","id":917128,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://kazuya-akimoto.com/2008/2008images/IMG_7608_8-headed_japanese_dragon.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">what would an ocean be without a monster lurking in the dark? it would be like sleep without dreams.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:03:07-07:00","id":917511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=917078#post917078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well that sounds friggin awesome, but this argument has been taken to the PM's to avoid causing any further drama.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, here's Bill Cipher doing some Fae related shenanigans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_9CY_B5hLo\" data-code=\"r_9CY_B5hLo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/r_9CY_B5hLo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> Is it said I thought you meant the Prime Minister for a minute.<br /> <br /> Its been a long day in the heat for me, and so I'm still addled.<br /> <br /> One thing I picture when picturing the True Fae is Jared from Labyrinth, varous Gods of Mythlogies, and weirdly the God of the Old Testament, who does some horrible things to to some people, and miracles to others, whose rules and behaviors seem baffling at times.<br /> <br /> I not looking to start an arguement on religion, I can just see a True Fae emulating that, or trying too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:04:08-07:00","id":917513,"title":"","content":"Another one, the Trickster from Supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:21:58-07:00","id":917527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=917511#post917511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it said I thought you meant the Prime Minister for a minute.<br /> <br /> Its been a long day in the heat for me, and so I'm still addled.<br /> <br /> One thing I picture when picturing the True Fae is Jared from Labyrinth, varous Gods of Mythlogies, and weirdly the God of the Old Testament, who does some horrible things to to some people, and miracles to others, whose rules and behaviors seem baffling at times.<br /> <br /> I not looking to start an argument on religion, I can just see a True Fae emulating that, or trying too.</div> </div> </div> </div> In-universe, I prefer to think of YHWH as a Rank 5 Guardian Angel that absorbed too much of the &quot;might makes right&quot; mentality that permeated the cultures at the time, turning Him into a well-meaning but extremely merciless <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/246019-primer-corrupted-programs-aberrations-of-the-god-machine\"><b>Aberrant</b></a> Exile. He seemed omnipotent and omniscient because humans were not capable of comprehending His Sufficiently Advanced technological powers. Or perhaps he was a magath spirit of similar Rank and function. No disrespect meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:33:34-07:00","id":917580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=917511#post917511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it said I thought you meant the Prime Minister for a minute.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Said&quot; or &quot;sad?&quot; No, on both counts.<br /> <br /> Anyways, he pretty much acts like a True Fae every time he appears throughout the series. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here's a clip of what happens when he manages to cross over into the physical plane!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ot3h6yY46Go\" data-code=\"Ot3h6yY46Go\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ot3h6yY46Go/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-19-2016, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T16:15:48-07:00","id":917604,"title":"","content":"I really like to think of the titular artifact from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mask\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Mask</b></a> as a Title in Prop form that turns the wearer into a pseudo Actor. After all, the wearers pursue their Vices and Aspirations with little thought for the consequences (Ruled By Passion), are all but invulnerable to mundane weapons (Immortal Flesh), develop a strong desire for mischief and/or cruelty and gain all sorts of bizarre magics. The <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GXsKPxBRXWI\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Cuban Pete</b></a> scene is a great example of Inciting Bedlam.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yes, I know the original Dark Horse version was way more violent and mean-spirited, but I prefer the idea that the Mask is more dangerous in the hands of certain people, rather than eventually turning everyone into a killer. Both versions can work in a CoD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-19-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T16:40:09-07:00","id":917619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class