hat quote under the illustration his or yours? It's really cool either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-19-2016, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T18:31:45-07:00","id":917692,"title":"","content":"...Okay, now I'm pretty sure I need to check out this Gravity Falls thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T19:45:32-07:00","id":917735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=917692#post917692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Okay, now I'm pretty sure I need to check out this Gravity Falls thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's a really good show, though I'd recommend avoiding any more spoilers before watching it; unraveling the mysteries and codes is part of the fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T00:25:00-07:00","id":917849,"title":"","content":"I apologize if this has been mentioned before, but I realized yesterday Kilgrave from Jessica Jones makes a good template for a True Fae. Uncaring, all-controlling master who holds delusions about what you need and just wants you back if you escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T04:14:02-07:00","id":917936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=917849#post917849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if this has been mentioned before, but I realized yesterday Kilgrave from Jessica Jones makes a good template for a True Fae. Uncaring, all-controlling master who holds delusions about what you need and just wants you back if you escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Kilgrave-like True Fae in Autumn Nightmares called the Grieve Of Stolen Lovers or the Gentleman, though he relies a lot more on actual charisma than emotion-controlling magic. And he has a 5 dot Token sword that becomes covered in silver fire and deals aggravated damage when activated. That sounds like something he'd use in a duel over a captive lover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T16:22:19-07:00","id":919992,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/rawhead_1515.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Characters/CourtneyCrumrinAndTheNightThingsNeutrals\" target=\"_blank\">Tommy Rawhead and Bloodybones</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T16:29:02-07:00","id":920623,"title":"","content":"It strikes me that <i>The Darkness</i> in Alan Wake is a perfect example of one of the True Fae.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I am older than you. Older than your first work of art. I will find a new face to wear. Someone else to dream me free.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> But what strikes me first is a sensation of <i>thusness</i>. The Fae describe and are described by their titles - thus they are thus and nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 06-24-2016, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T17:10:10-07:00","id":920635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=920623#post920623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It strikes me that <i>The Darkness</i> in Alan Wake is a perfect example of one of the True Fae.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I am older than you. Older than your first work of art. I will find a new face to wear. Someone else to dream me free.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> But what strikes me first is a sensation of <i>thusness</i>. The Fae describe and are described by their titles - thus they are thus and nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure if I understand. Are you talking about Titles like the ones of the Chaos Gods and Daedric Princes (e.g. She Who Thirsts, Shivering Isles)?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T18:03:09-07:00","id":920666,"title":"","content":"I'm talking their names. All of their names are titles.<br /> <br /> The maps describe the territory which describes the maps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:02:14-07:00","id":921644,"title":"","content":"For me, I've always described to others when pitching Changeling to imagine the True Fae like Jareth as a Cenobite.<br /> <br /> For me I always found it more terrible that the Keeper of the PCs has likely moved on and doesn't comprehend or care their latest toy (the PC) has actually left Arcadia. I've never really seen them as an antagonist outside of the backstory for PCs. I prefer to keep antagonists more Loyalist or Hedgebeast based. Nothing paints despair more when the PCs realise all their worrying about being hunted by their old Keeper is BS and they couldn't give a shit about them as they have new 'toys' now, especially a Winter courtier that's avoided living since they come back and they're not even being chased after...<br /> <br /> I am happy the Huntsman are being included now, as I like the added horror element that the changelings are being more clearly stalked by a more proactive antagonist linked to the True Fae now. I can't wait to learn more on them tbh as I'll likely play up them hunting the party very much to keep them on their toes and keep the game interesting when it goes into a lull. I think of the dog from The Thing for some reason when I think Huntsman, like a bloodhound that shape shifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:25:26-07:00","id":921659,"title":"","content":"When I think of Huntsmen, I imagine an unholy combination of Predator, Terminator, Kumihos and Treasure Mimics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T16:06:12-07:00","id":921735,"title":"","content":"Yeah, for sure I get the Kumiho vibe, especially of the more darker tales with them and the Treasure Mimic I get. I was selling people on the Huntsman by saying this;<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;So the changelings know they're gonna be hunted and y'know how as a kid you'd hide under the blankets of your bed to keep safe from monsters? Well tough luck, the bed itself turns out to be the monster and now it's carting you back to hell...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Speaking on being taken back to Hell, I've started to think of Frank from <i>Hellraiser</i> as a Darkling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> May have a puzzle box appear in a Goblin Market... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T06:18:34-07:00","id":921962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=921735#post921735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, for sure I get the Kumiho vibe, especially of the more darker tales with them and the Treasure Mimic I get. I was selling people on the Huntsman by saying this;<br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;So the changelings know they're gonna be hunted and y'know how as a kid you'd hide under the blankets of your bed to keep safe from monsters? Well tough luck, the bed itself turns out to be the monster and now it's carting you back to hell...&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> Speaking on being taken back to Hell, I've started to think of Frank from <i>Hellraiser</i> as a Darkling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> May have a puzzle box appear in a Goblin Market... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Awesome. I had an idea for a Darkling Hunterheart inspired by Pinhead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T20:26:21-07:00","id":927427,"title":"","content":"Huh.<br /> <br /> Going from the other direction, <i>this</i> is what it's like to be earthbound for the True Fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7ZxqhHhHFxI\" data-code=\"7ZxqhHhHFxI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7ZxqhHhHFxI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T22:07:24-07:00","id":929556,"title":"","content":"Pinhead as he appears in the first movie is classic True Fae. Before he was turned into a more standard demon, his whole deal of being an utterly inhuman hedonist from a realm of infinite pain but also infinite pleasure fits it perfectly. Hell, he even acts like a True Fae, dragging people into his personal realm and transforming them...<br /> <br /> Back to describing how we imagine the True Fae, I've always seen them as less &quot;completely random and unpredictable chaos beings&quot; and more of the &quot;living story&quot; idea. You know how spirits are described in both versions of WoD? That they do things because those things are part of their very nature, not because they decide to? Like, how a spirit of fire will always want to burn things, because that's what fire does, and it IS fire? The Gentry are like that for stories and archetypes. They seem chaotic, but they're actually very ordered (as shown by the fact that their powers are literal contracts). So, the Greve of Stolen Lovers seduces people not because he loves them, or even because he finds them attractive in any way. He seduces people because that's what handsome romantic heroes do. Seduction isn't just what he does, it's what he is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 07-18-2016, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T22:26:08-07:00","id":929560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=929556#post929556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pinhead as he appears in the first movie is classic True Fae. Before he was turned into a more standard demon, his whole deal of being an utterly inhuman hedonist from a realm of infinite pain but also infinite pleasure fits it perfectly. Hell, he even acts like a True Fae, dragging people into his personal realm and transforming them...<br /> <br /> Back to describing how we imagine the True Fae, I've always seen them as less &quot;completely random and unpredictable chaos beings&quot; and more of the &quot;living story&quot; idea. You know how spirits are described in both versions of WoD? That they do things because those things are part of their very nature, not because they decide to? Like, how a spirit of fire will always want to burn things, because that's what fire does, and it IS fire? The Gentry are like that for stories and archetypes. They seem chaotic, but they're actually very ordered (as shown by the fact that their powers are literal contracts). So, the Greve of Stolen Lovers seduces people not because he loves them, or even because he finds the attractive in any way. He seduces people because that's what handsome romantic heroes do. Seduction isn't just what he does, it's what he is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first time I ran Changeling I got really carried away by the whole &quot;infinite potential&quot; of the fae in general. Lots of weirdness and bizarre creatures, chimeras and horrors made largely from my own imagination. In retrospect I feel like it diluted the aesthetic. Too many creatures without any grounding in storytelling lessened the foundation of the setting. Basing each new creature, whether Hob, Fae, or Changeling, in a particular story or trope in some fashion would have gone a long way towards enhancing the game's flavour I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T06:58:52-07:00","id":929696,"title":"","content":"Greek gods","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T08:54:11-07:00","id":929763,"title":"","content":"Sorry to everyone for startung the argument about fanfic with my post. I myself feel that i have found some fanfic that is better than a lot of published stories and i should not have singled out fanfic writers, when the idea i was going for could really be applied to all writers. <br /> <br /> Anyway, i have a new &quot;what comes fo mind when i think of the Gentry&quot;: the &quot;teachers&quot; and the world of Don't Hug Me, I'm Scared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:31:18-07:00","id":929939,"title":"","content":"This may be a bit stereotypical of a choice, but as of late I've had a very strong idea for a space themed Gentry, particularly with their Changelings being stars, making up the &quot;backdrop&quot; of the darkness and even racing light for their freedom. As such, this is the kind of image I have for what such a Gentry would look like.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/leagueoflegends/images/c/c4/Thresh_DarkStarSkin.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20160602164920\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I do love League of Legends' skins. I may be missing the point of this thread though...again. :-p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T04:30:34-07:00","id":933360,"title":"","content":"The Daedra Princes of Oblivion are pretty much True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T10:11:13-07:00","id":933465,"title":"","content":"You know, I was working on my remake of Mage and briefly considered Lord English as an Abyssal entity (since he's all about destroying shit, and I'm giving the Abyss a very strong theme of &quot;breaking shit&quot;), but it hit me like a lightning bolt that he's 100% a True Fae. Not just in the sense that that's what he'd be, but he's a pretty perfect archetypal example of a powerful one- even including the fact that he considers himself a misunderstood genius but is really a terrible, derivative artist who just leeches off the talents of others. <br /> <br /> The way the reader learns about him is also a good model for revealing the True Fae- he initially appears as an unfathomable, utterly inhuman force of chaos, but as the story goes on the players learn about the particular set of rules he's bound to, and how his actions are primarily driven by petty jealousy and resentment. <br /> <br /> ...now I totally want to write up his stats, but I need Changeling 2e for that. (Assuming the rules are anything like Equinox Road, I'd say that Lord English, Caliborn, and Doc Scratch are his Actors, the Felt Mansion and the post-apocalyptic Medium are his realms, the Felt are his Wisps, and his Juju, his cane/rifle, his overcoat, and the ~ath server are his Props. (I haven't read ER in a while so I could be bungling it.)<br /> <br /> (Of course, his backstory is also that he was already part of a species of incredibly powerful magical beings before playing Sburb, which his species was never meant to do, and getting even more powerful. So in that way he's sort of like a True Fae that somehow learned to harness a piece of Infrastructure.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 07-18-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T11:58:38-07:00","id":933512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=933465#post933465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I was working on my remake of Mage and briefly considered Lord English as an Abyssal entity (since he's all about destroying shit, and I'm giving the Abyss a very strong theme of &quot;breaking shit&quot;), but it hit me like a lightning bolt that he's 100% a True Fae. Not just in the sense that that's what he'd be, but he's a pretty perfect archetypal example of a powerful one- even including the fact that he considers himself a misunderstood genius but is really a terrible, derivative artist who just leeches off the talents of others.<br /> <br /> The way the reader learns about him is also a good model for revealing the True Fae- he initially appears as an unfathomable, utterly inhuman force of chaos, but as the story goes on the players learn about the particular set of rules he's bound to, and how his actions are primarily driven by petty jealousy and resentment.<br /> <br /> ...now I totally want to write up his stats, but I need Changeling 2e for that. (Assuming the rules are anything like Equinox Road, I'd say that Lord English, Caliborn, and Doc Scratch are his Actors, the Felt Mansion and the post-apocalyptic Medium are his realms, the Felt are his Wisps, and his Juju, his cane/rifle, his overcoat, and the ~ath server are his Props. (I haven't read ER in a while so I could be bungling it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I LOVE this idea~ And from I remember of Equinox Road, a Gentry could only really have three titles active at once, at least in a feud; they could have a realm, actor and prop active, but not a house full of wisps as well.<br /> <br /> That said, they have changed certain things (Actors used to also be known as Huntsmen) so we'll see where this goes. But yes, yes yes yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T12:31:17-07:00","id":933526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=933512#post933512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And from I remember of Equinox Road, a Gentry could only really have three titles active at once, at least in a feud; they could have a realm, actor and prop active, but not a house full of wisps as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was an example of a Fae <i>with three Titles</i>, serving as a demonstrating of the fact that a Title can only be committed to one Manifestation at a time.<br /> <br /> Also the default maximum number of Titles you can have before Wyrd Transcendence is five; how many Titles you have determines how powerful all your Manifestations are. Not every object is a Prop, not every place is a Realm, and not every Manifestation in a story belongs to the same Fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Actors used to also be known as Huntsmen) </div> </div> </div>Nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T12:42:28-07:00","id":933532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=933512#post933512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Actors used to also be known as Huntsmen)</div> </div> </div> </div>There were Actors that were huntsmen, but never ever has there been a Huntsman prior to Second Edition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T13:58:31-07:00","id":933571,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, thank you for the correction. My memory of the supplement seems vague indeed to have made those errors. :-p My apologies for the misinformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T08:18:23-07:00","id":933901,"title":"","content":"Visually, the first images that come to mind are the Lady of Pain from D&amp;D's Planescape setting, Yubaba from Spirited Away, and for some reason the monster from M. Night Shyamalan's The Village. Obviously, each of these would just be a single physical manifestation of a greater entity. They also aren't my favorite images of Gentry, just the first ones called to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T14:46:58-07:00","id":1249790,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What springs to mind for me are the Golden Swan with Horns from the web-comic Year in Hereafter at <a href=\"http://www.yihcomic.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.yihcomic.com</a> and her antagonist Loviatar and the Upyr king from the web-comic Colorblind at cbcomic.smackjeeves.com. Both Loviatar and the Upyr king want to invade Earth. The Golden Swan with Horns doesn't want Loviatar to mess up Earth or at least Finland and uses the protagonists to defend it. The five children in Colorblind were apparently in the wrong place at the right time to get caught up in things. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In </span></span></span></div> <i>The Irish Celtic Magical Tradition </i> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">by Steve Blamires the author describes the Tuatha de Danann as starting out as fully fledged people but becoming two dimensional caricatures of themselves over time. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So that's my notion of the True Fae: a coalition of beings who like our ever changing world and create Changelings,</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Magi, Hunters, Etc. to defend it and because that's how they reproduce. </span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T01:57:14-07:00","id":1249904,"title":"","content":"Having invested myself more into second edition, when I think of Gentry I tend to think of pieces of media that I have vested interests in. For some reason, I like taking figures or places from them and put them through a Fae filter, and they tend to become the villains rather than playable protagonists. These include Doctor Who (both in the form of the Doctor and House from \u201cThe Doctor\u2019s Wife\u201d), Batman (or rather, Gotham City itself), Harry Potter (The Knight Bus is oddly compelling as a triple decker bus) and Carmen Sandiego herself, though that is only off the top of my head. Classic fae figures tend to be spurned by my imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 08-31-2018, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T03:22:52-07:00","id":1249918,"title":"","content":"The Dark Powers from Ranvenloft could be considered True Fae: they abduct the vilest evildoers, turn them into Dark Lords contained in mini-Domains on their own and inflict on them ironic curses as part of their eternal punishment. They are also oblivious to the plight of the inmocent people under the Lords' rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T16:37:02-07:00","id":1250094,"title":"","content":"To be completely honest, I don't see the majority of the True Fae as very likely keepers. When I think of the True Fae, I see huldras, John Bauer trolls, garden gnomes, and giants. I see N\u00e4cken sitting in a stream playing his violin, drowning kids who come too close. I see an old wizened man pointing out the way for kids lost in the woods, leading them more astray.<br /> While there are stories about trolls who actually kidnap people, especially babies, they're seldom a single keeper, but a family of trolls.<br /> All of these are of course very much related to nature. I really don't like the idea of urban fae, which is also why none of my changeling stories have been set in modern eras, but in 19th century, or earlier, Nordic villages. I also have a problem with the notion that the True Fae can turn into whatever they like, that they barely ever leave Arcadia and are basically gods while they're there. Even Loki needed a magical cape to be able to fly in the original stories.<br /> To me, True Fae are creatures with Wyrd. Some don't even form contracts.<br /> <br /> Then I saw Coraline and was like &quot;Ah. I get it now.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T18:13:21-07:00","id":1250112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spinnerling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1250094#post1250094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be completely honest, I don't see the majority of the True Fae as very likely keepers. When I think of the True Fae, I see huldras, John Bauer trolls, garden gnomes, and giants. I see N\u00e4cken sitting in a stream playing his violin, drowning kids who come too close. I see an old wizened man pointing out the way for kids lost in the woods, leading them more astray.<br /> While there are stories about trolls who actually kidnap people, especially babies, they're seldom a single keeper, but a family of trolls.<br /> All of these are of course very much related to nature. I really don't like the idea of urban fae, which is also why none of my changeling stories have been set in modern eras, but in 19th century, or earlier, Nordic villages. I also have a problem with the notion that the True Fae can turn into whatever they like, that they barely ever leave Arcadia and are basically gods while they're there. Even Loki needed a magical cape to be able to fly in the original stories.<br /> To me, True Fae are creatures with Wyrd. Some don't even form contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of those sound more like hobgoblins rather than True Fae when it comes to how Changeling handles things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T18:57:13-07:00","id":1250124,"title":"","content":"The first thing I think about is their depiction in Gargoyles. How they can take shapes we do not associate with the Fae to weave legends (like the Banshee), of how they leave behind artifacts of power to propel new tales (like Odin and Anubis), or how some oppose each other and people never realize its one of their contests (like Grandmother and Coyote). Some get so caught up by their passions or projects that they dedicate a lifetime to them (like Puck) and even the most benevolent looking may be very manipulative (such as Titania). When dealing with them, sometimes they can be petty and unreasonable, throwing their might around in a tantrum to get what they want, but still giving just enough leeway to cut a deal (like Oberon). Others can provide aid when impressed (like Puck), while some are bound by ancient rules (such as The Gathering) and can only give cryptic hints that further their plans while seemingly giving aid (like Titania with the iron bell). They are also patient, so very patient, after all, &quot;what is time to an immortal ?&quot; They can set up plans eons in advance, manipulating events with seductive promises of power or vengeance, twisting and binding destinies as they set up the acts in their play (such as the Weird Sisters). Sure, there is a lot of room for spontaneity and improvisation, but the key is to remember they have much longer to prepare a conflict that will become worth remembering before the curtain downs on the performance.<br /> <br /> The second thing I associate with them is the feel that what they present should be alien and enticing. Termina from Majora's Mask and the movie Spirited Away capture this for me. Their domains are alien, but still familiar enough to present a sense of wonder, to tempt you into exploring its multifarious aspects, to partake in this mysteries, even if its only brought forth in as humble a form as an artifact.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I feel they embody the fear of the unknown, the moment where the character learns their understanding was not enough. This could happen when one of their plans comes into fruition, or when they remember a moment of the Durance or discover themselves ensnared by a Charlatan's trap with no knowledge of the taboos they abide by. Much like in the Cthulu Mythos, the fear of what we cannot comprehend, the madness of fruitlessly attempting to grasp its sideways logic, the constant paranoia of what horrors hide beyond the senses, silent before they pounce, those are also key aspects of The Gentry.<br /> <br /> To me, the True Fae are made by different compositions of those 3 ingredients.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-30-2018, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T10:54:01-07:00","id":1250485,"title":"","content":"I get a multi-tiered image of the True Fae, due to both my readings in mythology and folklore on the one side and reading a lot of game settings and systems on the other. First up comes a lot of imagery from Scottish &amp; Irish tales -- Daoine Sidhe, Fomorians, Redcaps, Balor and all of that ilk. Then I mix in a couple of bits of the Norse -- alfar, svartalfar, giants (of frost or fire, depending). Then there is a small dose of demons of various types. <br /> <br /> From <i>Ars Magica</i> I picked up the notion of faeries being shaped by the stories that humans tell; in this concept, the Others are not terribly creative, while humans are. This gives them impetus to grab up humans (The Lost) as they are looking for a certain amount of novelty. This also allows for more modern imagery to creep in -- alien invaders, notions of computers gone mad, slasher villains, etc. But it also means that The Others are always a bit ... off. They are dong a fair amount of mix n match, so there are jagged edges, contradictions and confusion. <br /> <br /> Bundle this up with modern folklore, urban legends, and some of the ... more singular ... ideas that crop up on the internet, and somewhere in there I triangulate on The Others.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, they are weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T05:46:33-07:00","id":1250717,"title":"","content":"Ever seen that Torchwood episode with the fairies? <br /> <br /> It was called Small Worlds, and basically there were these creepy green... things which took a child and killed every last person who tried to resist.<br /> <br /> That is a True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T11:44:32-07:00","id":1253333,"title":"","content":"Target Practice.<br /> <br /> Everyone thinks that a nigh unkillable opponent is a very bad thing. I disagree: True Fae being uber-powerful just means I can go full Madman on them with Katastrofi 5-Dot Void Cannons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T16:03:52-07:00","id":1253731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae#post910526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I guess my favorite True Fae tend to be like Disney villains to some degree, but with a strong eldritch dose.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, Bill Cipher, then?<br /> <br /> <br /> I like to imagine the True Fae as entities who never learned how to deal with disappointment. Whatever it is that originally spawned the True Fae spoiled them to the point where they have grown accustomed to always getting their way. Hell, another word for them is <i>&quot;Gentry&quot;</i> which is just a fancy way of saying <i>&quot;Nobility.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> When your average, every day citizen violates the law, chances are they'll face consequences for their actions. But if a wealthy, popular, or important citizen does the same crime, there's a good chance they'll walk away with a mere slap on the wrist.<br /> <br /> True Fae are like that, except they can get away with violating the <b>laws of reality.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T19:13:03-07:00","id":1307653,"title":"","content":"If we treat the Anunnaki from Zecharia Sitchin's Earth Chronicles as True Fae we can say that they lived openly among us until the early iron age. As we continue to replace iron and steel with aluminum, plastic and fiberglass we can expect their return. In the Earth Chronicles books we have three basic factions: serpent, eagle, and lion representing Enki, Enlil, and Inanna. It's easy to imagine the Nations of the United States (Eagle), China (Serpent/Dragon), and Russia (Lion/Bear) as proxies for these three factions.<br /> <br /> As an aside I once read the prophecy &quot;The Goat God and the Antelope God contend for the throne of Heaven&quot;. I can't remember what book I read that in though I think the identities of the Goat God and Antelope god can be found in Lewis Spence's work on Babylonian Mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","user":"moonwolf8","date":".  Oops, I originally wrote content instead of contend. My bad. 04-25-2019, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T05:05:46-07:00","id":1309412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1250112#post1250112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of those sound more like hobgoblins rather than True Fae when it comes to how Changeling handles things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that's my biggest beef with CtL. I love to use True Fae as villains against mortals - tricking them to sign pledges, or sending them to Arcadia, or outright killing them - as the stories of old. Peter Pan, the old woman from Beauty and the Beast who turns the castle, malevolent genies in bottles, Santa Claus.<br /> <br /> Skipping the part of the story where the mortal meets the fae is just a great waste to me. For me, the focus should be about entering and surviving Arcadia, not the aftermath of leaving it. Changeling sometimes feels like the sequel to a film nobody's seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T05:29:04-07:00","id":1309415,"title":"","content":"The True Fae? GMs and rpg players. Particularly after reading Equinox Road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T09:43:09-07:00","id":1309464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spinnerling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1309412#post1309412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that's my biggest beef with CtL. I love to use True Fae as villains against mortals - tricking them to sign pledges, or sending them to Arcadia, or outright killing them - as the stories of old. Peter Pan, the old woman from Beauty and the Beast who turns the castle, malevolent genies in bottles, Santa Claus.<br /> <br /> Skipping the part of the story where the mortal meets the fae is just a great waste to me. For me, the focus should be about entering and surviving Arcadia, not the aftermath of leaving it. Changeling sometimes feels like the sequel to a film nobody's seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of other games that tell that sort of story, though. Why bother treading old ground when there's so much more beyond the horizon of &quot;Happily Ever After&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T10:17:10-07:00","id":1309468,"title":"","content":", <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spinnerling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1309412#post1309412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that's my biggest beef with CtL. I love to use True Fae as villains against mortals - tricking them to sign pledges, or sending them to Arcadia, or outright killing them - as the stories of old. Peter Pan, the old woman from Beauty and the Beast who turns the castle, malevolent genies in bottles, Santa Claus.<br /> <br /> Skipping the part of the story where the mortal meets the fae is just a great waste to me. For me, the focus should be about entering and surviving Arcadia, not the aftermath of leaving it. Changeling sometimes feels like the sequel to a film nobody's seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize that is why the hedge and hobgoblins and hedge-ghosts exist right? You can have fae of tonnes of different sorts in changeling, it's just true fae are grander than just things like huldra, trolls, garden gnomes, and giants. True Fae are citadels of the giants, armies of trolls, the king of gnomes, the huldra that seduced winter, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T12:59:52-07:00","id":1309494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spinnerling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1309412#post1309412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that's my biggest beef with CtL. I love to use True Fae as villains against mortals - tricking them to sign pledges, or sending them to Arcadia, or outright killing them - as the stories of old. Peter Pan, the old woman from Beauty and the Beast who turns the castle, malevolent genies in bottles, Santa Claus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fun Fact: in the original story of Aladdin, the Genies were servants to Rocs. The reason why Aladdin ran out of wishes was because he asked the Genie to kidnap a Roc egg for him, which they took as a grievous insult!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T18:59:49-07:00","id":1310645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1309494#post1309494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Fun Fact: in the original story of Aladdin, the Genies were servants to Rocs. The reason why Aladdin ran out of wishes was because he asked the Genie to kidnap a Roc egg for him, which they took as a grievous insult!</div> </div> </div> </div>Rocs? like the big eagles/hawks? hmm, didnt know that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T20:44:57-07:00","id":1310664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1310645#post1310645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rocs? like the big eagles/hawks? hmm, didnt know that</div> </div> </div> </div>Try bird of prey so big that it feeds full-grown elephants to its chicks like worms. Plus, apparently has magic besides the magic that lets it so flagrantly violate the square-cube law. <br /> <br /> Only being of the air spoken of in the Middle East that is bigger is Ziz, Lord of the Skies, ruler of all that flies and similarly-sized cousin to Behemoth and Leviathan. I'm pretty sure he eats rocs for breakfast","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-07-2019, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T21:30:29-07:00","id":1310674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1310645#post1310645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rocs? like the big eagles/hawks? hmm, didnt know that</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, the original story is far different from the Disney one.<br /> <br /> Alladin is an incompetent buffoon, who desperately needs the Genie's help to do anything right. He's also not bound by a 3 wish limit, and is presumably able to have an unlimited number of wishes granted, until he makes the mistake of wishing for a Roc's egg. That's the final straw that makes the Genie decide to up and leave his ass. I presume that shortly after this incident, all the fame and fortune Alladin had amassed through the Genie's power quickly begins to dry up, and he's back to being an impoverished thief once more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T11:14:32-07:00","id":1311016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1309468#post1309468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">,<br /> You realize that is why the hedge and hobgoblins and hedge-ghosts exist right? You can have fae of tonnes of different sorts in changeling, it's just true fae are grander than just things like huldra, trolls, garden gnomes, and giants. True Fae are citadels of the giants, armies of trolls, the king of gnomes, the huldra that seduced winter, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to say that changelings themselves are faeries but that their anglophone jargon seems to have a bias against the idea, hence the &quot;true&quot; monicker. By contrast, compare the reference to &quot;elves and elven-kings&quot; in the Iceland section from the new corebook. I came up with the expression of &quot;higher/lower fae&quot; to refer to this. In fact, I think one of my favourite things in the game is that there isn't a black and white division between humanity and faeries but an espectrum of sorts, and the faerie world is full of many different kind of things that we can call fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T16:37:00-07:00","id":1311094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1311016#post1311016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like to say that changelings themselves are faeries but that their anglophone jargon seems to have a bias against the idea, hence the &quot;true&quot; monicker. By contrast, compare the reference to &quot;elves and elven-kings&quot; in the Iceland section from the new corebook. I came up with the expression of &quot;higher/lower fae&quot; to refer to this. In fact, I think one of my favourite things in the game is that there isn't a black and white division between humanity and faeries but an espectrum of sorts, and the faerie world is full of many different kind of things that we can call fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really understand how this relates with the statement you quoted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T02:15:52-07:00","id":1311186,"title":"","content":"I think I was too sleepy to make sense of it :s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T20:41:07-07:00","id":1311332,"title":"","content":"When I think of the True Fae I think of the Primordial Gods spoken of in Hesiod's Theogony. These are beings that are functional worlds, objects, people, and nature combined into a single will that pulls itself into existance from nothing but its own will to exist. <br /> <br /> Take Gods like Chaos, Tartarus, Gaia, Nyx, Ererubus, Hermara, Aether. Compared to the Titans and Olypmians the Primal Greek Olds are alien, Fey even. Beings dwell within them, yet they still when they choose can take anthromorphic forms when they choose. <br /> <br /> I've never understood why the Greeks saw Chaos as a Goddess that created the Universe, but built no temples to her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T22:56:06-07:00","id":1311339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1311332#post1311332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never understood why the Greeks saw Chaos as a Goddess that created the Universe, but built no temples to her.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the saying goes, creators are only truly appreciated after they're dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T00:21:24-07:00","id":1311357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1311332#post1311332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never understood why the Greeks saw Chaos as a Goddess that created the Universe, but built no temples to her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chaos was never a goddess, maybe genderless and shapeless.<br /> <br /> ''The Night left the Cosmic Egg in Erebus, when Chaos, Gaia, Tartarus (Gaia's viscera) and Eros were created. In other versions, Chaos existed before all, and from this his children were created, Gaia, Tartarus, Eros or Phanis, Night and Erebus.<br /> <br /> Chaos = infinity, emptiness, void, the inconceivable<br /> Erebus = absolute darkness, Gaia = earth, Eros - Phanis = love - light<br /> Nyx (night) was born of Chaos and was the mother of the following entities:Erebos<br /> Ether<br /> Day<br /> Grace<br /> Styx <br /> Sleep<br /> Death<br /> Forward ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 05-11-2019, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T09:01:24-07:00","id":1311393,"title":"","content":"Note that Greek <i>\u03a7\u1f71\u03bf\u03c2</i> means &quot;void&quot; or &quot;emptiness&quot;; according to Hesiod, Erebus and Nyx &quot;came into being out of the void&quot;, while Aether and Hemera then &quot;were conceived after joining in love&quot;. I don't see chaos as a creator so much as a medium that other things arose from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T09:14:52-07:00","id":1311398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1309464#post1309464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of other games that tell that sort of story, though. Why bother treading old ground when there's so much more beyond the horizon of &quot;Happily Ever After&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there though? I mean one reason for WoD/CoD to have a core book is for vanilla mortals to find all the things in the Darkness, but I can't say I have seen many pen &amp; paper games surrounding the courts of the Fae outside Changeling - and barely even <i>in</i> Changeling. CtL focuses on life outside of Arcadia, and Tolkien elves take the Fae's place in most other games.<br /> I'm not very well-versed in games, though, so I'd gladly take recommendations of such games in a PM if you know some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T09:18:54-07:00","id":1311399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/910526-what-first-comes-to-your-mind-when-you-think-of-the-true-fae?p=1309468#post1309468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">,<br /> You realize that is why the hedge and hobgoblins and hedge-ghosts exist right? You can have fae of tonnes of different sorts in changeling, it's just true fae are grander than just things like huldra, trolls, garden gnomes, and giants. True Fae are citadels of the giants, armies of trolls, the king of gnomes, the huldra that seduced winter, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're quite right at that. Maybe I just haven't seen them used that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T11:25:14-07:00","id":1311411,"title":"","content":"Clive Barker's Hell Priest.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am slightly odd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T08:43:17-07:00","id":1315882,"title":"","content":"When I think about the Gentry and the Keeper two things come to my mind.<br /> <br /> First, the Narcissistic Personality Disorder (NPD). Fae are in their essence emotional vampires. They harvest glamour through emotion, the more intense the better, so do changeling. They care nothing about you, your suffering, your adoration, your whatever; your emotions are their meal.<br /> <br /> Second, they need you. There is something in the human being that changelings were that was useful for them. Perhaps a book can only be read under the light of true love and your love for your child fits perfectly. Or your biased sense of justice could make you a perfect assassin. Or your voice has the perfect vibration to help your Keeper sleep. There is something in you that makes you necessary for them. One way or another, they need you, so in yourself and your durance are lots of answers about the Keeper and yourself. I find this last point of view the more interesting from a narrative perspective and character buildup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 06-01-2019, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}